{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The 1/4-20 machine screws felt useful because they could pair with my recent 1/4-20 rivet nuts, provided the length fits the material I am fastening.",
    "The insulated connectors and disposable gloves fit practical repair and workshop tasks: connectors could support wiring repairs, while suitable gloves would help with messy work."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The valve, pressure gauge and pipe nipples require specific plumbing applications I do not currently have; owning workshop tools does not create a need for those fittings.",
    "Foam gun cleaner does not follow from my tape and epoxy use because I have no current expanding-foam task. Another wood screw assortment also feels unnecessary when I already have a substantial kit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in hardware seems to have been stretched into an assumed need for plumbing parts, even though their uses differ from my recent fastening projects.",
    "My previous purchases of screws and adhesives seem to count too strongly without considering whether an item adds something useful or serves the same kind of task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters to me: thread size, screw length, head shape and wire gauge determine whether an otherwise relevant item is usable.",
    "I distinguish useful additions from supplies I already own or materials that need a specific project. The metric screws and mesh interest me, but I would wait for a concrete need."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my hands-on repair interests but sometimes mistake broad workshop relevance for a compatible, timely need."
}"}
